WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:04.488
- [Giselle] Girl Scout cookies,

00:00:04.488 --> 00:00:07.011
Kellogg's cafe, second floor!

00:00:07.011 --> 00:00:07.844
- [Girl] Yes, come on!

00:00:07.844 --> 00:00:09.261
We sell all of it, we sell all of them!

00:00:09.944 --> 00:00:10.777
- Awesome!

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:12.660
Show them the way,
girls, show them the way!

00:00:15.959 --> 00:00:18.832
You having fun? You need more cards?

00:00:18.832 --> 00:00:19.665
Go ahead.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.980
For me, being a part of this movement

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.646
gave me that sense of feeling empowered.

00:00:25.646 --> 00:00:26.938
- I'm done, I'm done, I'm done!

00:00:26.938 --> 00:00:27.771
- I'm done, yes!

00:00:27.771 --> 00:00:30.790
- What I have done with this troop

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:32.480
has definitely opened up something

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:34.920
that's been dormant in a lot
of people for a long time,

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.010
and that's doing the right thing.

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:39.590
- [Woman] Ah, that's my favorite cookie!

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:40.598
- [Girl] I'm not the favorite?

00:00:40.598 --> 00:00:42.240
(girls laughing)

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:43.780
- They're bringing 'em in.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:45.119
Oh god.

00:00:45.119 --> 00:00:48.870
I'm out of breath. (laughs)

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:50.263
I didn't even walk that far.

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:52.810
(soft uplifting music)

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:54.550
When you're in a traditional
Girl Scouting troop,

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:57.150
it's easy for you to go to
your meetings every week.

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:00.593
They can see normal faces
that you see every day.

00:01:02.064 --> 00:01:02.930
But when you're in the shelter system,

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:03.930
you don't have that.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.430
There is no stability.

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:08.260
You don't know if you'll
be there for long.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:10.444
You don't know when you'll be moved again.

00:01:10.444 --> 00:01:13.861
(mellow uplifting music)

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.770
Troop 6000 is the first
Girl Scouting troop

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:20.080
that's solely made for girls

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.630
who are living in the New
York City shelter system.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:27.630
There are about 8,000 homeless
girls living in New York City

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:30.020
who are of Girl Scouting age.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:31.603
So, for now, my dream is

00:01:31.603 --> 00:01:34.073
to be able to reach all 8,000 girls.

00:01:41.997 --> 00:01:43.800
Jade, go sit on the sofa, please?

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:45.280
Jade, go sit on the sofa, please.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:47.023
We're gonna do our homework over here.

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:49.930
Put the paint on that side of the table.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.650
You see the line there?

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:54.029
So, that's the mountain...

00:01:54.029 --> 00:01:55.020
- Yeah.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:55.853
You can paint that.

00:01:55.853 --> 00:01:57.143
And then you paint the sun.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.000
My children and I ended
up in a shelter in 2016

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.960
because our home was sold
to make way for new condos

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:07.060
that were being built.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.750
Trying to find a home in New
York City with five children

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.055
is almost near impossible.

00:02:12.055 --> 00:02:15.232
(soft dramatic music)

00:02:15.624 --> 00:02:17.765
I found myself with my
back against the wall

00:02:17.765 --> 00:02:20.486
and now idea of how to get out of it.

00:02:20.486 --> 00:02:23.183
So, we ended up in the
shelter in Long Island City.

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:28.150
My kids had no one to talk to about it

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:30.550
and felt like they
couldn't let anyone know,

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:31.650
felt ashamed about it.

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:35.680
When children are in the
shelter system, especially,

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.720
they don't have the things
that they're used to having

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:38.553
in their lives.

00:02:38.553 --> 00:02:39.410
A lot of things are changing.

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:40.835
There's no stability for them.

00:02:40.835 --> 00:02:42.743
So it can seem scary.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.900
It hurts.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:47.420
You feel, in a way, that
you've let your children down,

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:49.730
even though you tried
everything that you could.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:51.060
When you see your children like that,

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.860
it makes you feel helpless.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:55.880
So you just have to, as a
parent, hold yourself together

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:58.280
and be as brave as you
can possibly be for them.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:07.920
I worked for Girl Scouts
of Greater New York

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.500
prior to becoming homeless.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.550
My job was to start new troops
and recruit new Girl Scouts.

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:16.960
So, when I landed in the
shelter, I did what I knew best.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.240
And that was to go back

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:20.510
and ask if I could start a troop there.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:22.750
I knew first hand how important
it was for these girls

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:24.920
to have the Girl Scout experience.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:26.339
- [Girl Scout] On my honor...

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:27.759
- [Girls In Unison] On my honor...

00:03:27.759 --> 00:03:28.932
- [Girl Scout] I will try...

00:03:28.932 --> 00:03:30.450
- [Girls In Unison] I will try...

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:31.440
- [Girl Scout] To serve God...

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.620
- [Girls In Unison] To serve God...

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:33.850
- [Girl Scout] And my country...

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:35.080
- [Girls In Unison] And my country..

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.050
- To help people...

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:37.270
- [Girls In Unison] To help people...

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:38.103
- At all times.

00:03:38.103 --> 00:03:39.171
- [Girls In Unison] At all times.

00:03:39.171 --> 00:03:40.004
- [Girl Scout] And to live...

00:03:40.004 --> 00:03:41.010
- [Girls In Unison] And to live...

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:41.950
- By the Girl Scout Law.

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:43.933
- [Girls In Unison] By the Girl Scout Law.

00:03:43.933 --> 00:03:45.600
- Excellent, all right,
everyone take a seat.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:46.753
Thank you so much.

00:03:49.633 --> 00:03:51.550
(mellow uplifting music)

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:54.313
- I started Troop 6000
in February of 2017.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:59.300
From our first troop of 17
girls, including my three,

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:00.680
we've expanded city wide.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:03.023
We're now at 362 girls.

00:04:04.563 --> 00:04:06.251
- [Troop Leader] Is everyone
holding someone else's hand?

00:04:06.251 --> 00:04:07.084
- [Girls In Unison] Yeah.

00:04:07.084 --> 00:04:10.210
- Girls are meeting at
their shelters once a week

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:11.330
for an hour and a half.

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:13.580
Same day, same time, every week.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:16.023
Again, instilling that
stability for the girls.

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:23.210
We teach girls robotics
to civic engagement,

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:26.960
to building their business
with the cookie program.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:29.190
These girls go back to their parents

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:30.540
at the end of the meetings

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:33.460
very bright eyed and cheerful
and letting their parents know

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:34.600
that they've done so much.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:37.360
And that things are gonna be fine.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:38.760
Things are gonna get better.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:43.300
It's important for them to
build that sisterly bond,

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:45.023
to know that they're not alone.

00:04:48.851 --> 00:04:51.850
(uplifting bright music)

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:55.013
- My name is Sanaa and I'm
a member of Troop 6000.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.700
I have been a member since
the very first meeting.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:03.370
Living in the shelter, it was very quiet.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:06.813
I didn't have people to play
with, except for my brothers.

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:10.853
Usually, I would just play
with my toys by myself.

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:17.540
When the Girl Scouts came, I was excited,

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:20.070
'cause then finally, I
wouldn't have to be bored

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:21.910
all the time.

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:23.950
When I started talking to the girls,

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:26.460
I started to feel like I wasn't alone

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:29.140
and I had people dealing
with the same problem.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:32.180
Two tagalongs, four Thin
Mints, and one Trefoil.

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:34.400
Girls can be whoever they want to be,

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.990
no matter the problems they have

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:40.450
or the difficulties they're dealing with.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:45.270
Troop 6000 was designed
for girls to stay in it,

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:47.890
no matter if they were
in a shelter or not.

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:50.540
Once you're a Girl Scout,
you're always a Girl Scout.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:55.760
- [Giselle] Jalessi,
you want chicken, right?

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:56.593
- [Jalessi] Yeah.

00:05:56.593 --> 00:05:58.543
- Okay, come sit down Jalessi.

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:02.473
Haley, don't spill it.

00:06:04.773 --> 00:06:07.840
Go ahead, Jessi.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:09.932
- Forever and ever, every night, amen.

00:06:09.932 --> 00:06:10.765
- Go ahead, Jay.

00:06:10.765 --> 00:06:12.793
- Thank you Jesus, I help you pray.

00:06:12.793 --> 00:06:15.519
I help you pray for Jesus and amen.

00:06:15.519 --> 00:06:17.363
- Amen.

00:06:17.363 --> 00:06:18.342
- [Child] I'm already eating.

00:06:18.342 --> 00:06:19.230
- You're already eating?

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:20.897
I know, I'm hungry too.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:24.200
(uplifting piano music)

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.080
After being in a shelter for a year,

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:27.653
we're now living in a home.

00:06:29.673 --> 00:06:30.890
It feels great.

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:33.420
But then again, I still
can't help but think about

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:35.620
those who are still
waiting for their homes.

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:38.200
When I was at my lowest

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:41.500
and felt like I had no
one there to support me,

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:44.760
Girl Scouting definitely was there for me.

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:46.510
I wanted to make sure that no other girls

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:48.260
felt the way that my daughters did.

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:52.260
- She taught me how to stand up for myself

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:55.200
and to believe in what I think is right

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:56.463
and to never give up.

00:06:57.350 --> 00:07:00.230
- We're giving them a
different type of family.

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:02.310
We definitely want to uplift them and

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:03.840
let them know that this
moment in their life

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:05.360
doesn't define them.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:06.330
(uplifting music)

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:08.070
There will be setbacks in life,

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:10.700
whether we expect them
or we don't expect them.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:13.570
It doesn't mean that
we're not worth anything,

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:15.373
that we've messed up in life.

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:19.720
I want for my daughters
and for the other girls

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:20.930
who are in Girl Scouting

00:07:20.930 --> 00:07:23.410
to grow up in a world where the future

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:25.110
is going to be limitless for them.

